Your AI coding assistant just generated the following JavaScript utility for an age-gate feature. Your task is to **review the code critically** and identify every bug before it reaches production.

The function is supposed to:
- Accept an array of user objects (each has at least a `name` field; `age` may or may not be present)
- Return a new array containing only users who are **strictly over 18** (i.e., age must be > 18, not >= 18)
- Users with a missing or non-numeric `age` field must be **excluded** from the result

Here is the generated code:

```javascript
// users.js
function filterAdults(users) {
  return users.filter(user => {
    const age = user.age;
    if (age >= 18) {
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  });
}

module.exports = { filterAdults };
```

List every bug you find, explain why each one is wrong, and write the corrected version of the function.

